  "_ad1_025_comment": "AD1-025 Omnimon prints [Assembly] -6 [WarGreymon] x [MetalGarurumon] (DCGO AD1_025.cs:214-255 AddAssemblyConditionClass, reduceCost 6, elements WarGreymon x1 + MetalGarurumon x1) but the digimoncard.io ingest dropped it. This override restores the keyword on effect_description_eng (engine play behavior is driven by the assembly alt_path in cards/ad1/AD1-025.yaml). Reminder text phrased per Comprehensive Rules section 7-3; the official English parenthetical was not recoverable from a primary source.",
  "AD1-025": {
    "effect_description_eng": "[Assembly] -6 [WarGreymon] x [MetalGarurumon]\n(You may play this card by placing the specified cards from your trash under it as its digivolution cards, reducing the play cost by the specified amount.)\n＜Raid＞ (When this Digimon attacks, you may switch the target of attack to 1 of your opponent's unsuspended Digimon with the highest DP.)\r\n＜Blocker＞ (This Digimon can block in the blocker timing.)\r\n＜Partition ([WarGreymon] & [MetalGarurumon])＞ (When this Digimon with each of the specified digivolution cards would leave the battle area other than by your own effects or by battle, you may play 1 each of the specified cards without paying the costs.)\r\n[On Play] [When Digivolving] Return all of your opponent's Digimon with as many or fewer digivolution cards as this Digimon to the bottom of the deck. Then, delete 1 of your opponent's Digimon.\r\n[All Turns] [Once Per Turn] When any of your opponent's Digimon leave the battle area, trash 1 of their Option cards in the battle area and trash their top security card.",
    "evo_costs": [
